The SBB is the Storageworks option> No good to you unless you have a BAXXXX
typ storageworks box to house it in. The other MAY be ok. It depends on the
extrention after TLZ06_xx where XX is the extention. A " TLZ06-DA " would
be a standalone table top model. You would need the external SCSI cable to
connect it to your 3100. An " TLZ06-AA" wouyld be the internally mounted
model. This mounts inside the 3100 and you remove the plastic plate at the
front of the 3100 for tape access. The cables for this are already inside
your 3100 unless you have filled all of the SCSI mount positions with
disks.....Hope this helps. PS I have a TLZ06-DA on my PC which works
fine,,,,

