I have inherited a MicroVax II with a bad console port. It will accept
characters (as I can login and run under VMS, although blind), but will
not output anything to the console terminal.  This is the second CPU
in this system that has had this behavior.

I don't know if it is the CPU board itself or the interface/battery unit
that it plugs into (but I have 2 sets to play with).

Is this a common fault on MVII's that is fixable (soldering iron OK),
or is the only fix a new CPU board? Are there any schematics for the
CPU available on the internet?



