If you're going the *nix route, I have to insert a plug for NetBSD
here...  it runs like a champ on my (headless) 3000/400.  The only
drawback I see for you is that X isn't quite supported yet.  (Console
support for the framebuffer just recently got added, and X has been
running on the TurboChannel MIPS DECStations for a while now...)
NetBSD supports running OSF^WDU^WTru64 binaries, so it's forseeable at
least that their compiler would run under it too.

Best of all it's free, liberally licensed, and of course you get the
source.  I've also heard rumors of linux folks trying to port to
turbochannel alphas, although I have no idea how far along it is...
maybe somebody else here can fill us in?
