>Tom Combs (combs@magnet.fsu.edu) wrote:

>:    What is this?  I now need a license for fcntl??? 

No - "register" in this case means register with portmap.  See
rpcinfo(8), a very useful tool for checking the health of NFS-related
daemons.

>No, you have to re-start rpc.lockd, which either had not been
>started at all, or died for some reason. 

VERY important: And start rpc.statd!  Lockd goes nowhere until it finds
statd.

If you didn't configure NFS to use locking, you should do that to automatically
start statd and lockd.

