News wrote:
> 
> Is it possible to upgrade an Alphastation 255 to NT,
> and if so how?...

The AS255 only has 512KB of flash.  This is enough to hold either the
SRM console or the ARC console, but not both at the same time.

Boot the firmware CDROM.  When you update the firmware, some versions
will ask whether you want to install the SRM or ARC (AlphaBIOS).  If it
doesn't ask, use the command "UPDATE ARC" instead of just "UPDATE".

NOTE: If you just want occassional access to ARC, it is possible to
build a floppy that you can boot to flip you over to ARC without
removing the SRM.

It is also possible to load an image from the network which will do the
same thing.  Look for ABBOOT.SYS.

Good luck!

