In article <38169BD1.3F13A2B5@anl.com.au>,
Paul Dudley  <dudleyp@anl.com.au> wrote:
> We have moved our two AS4100's from an old 10Mbps co-axial
> ethernet to a 100Mbps Twisted-Pair full duplex network. However
> the servers look like they are still talking to the network at 10 Mbps.
> How can we force them to talk at 100 Mbps? Note that the two are
> running RAID disk software and asemgr.

From Digital UNIX:

	ifconfig tu0 speed 100

Put the "speed 100" option in the rc.config line for the 100btx port.

You probably also want to set it in SRM too:

	>>> set ewa0_mode fast

Don't try for full duplex. That doesn't seem to be a good thing on DEC gear.

If you're running VMS, I think this'll do it:

	$ MCR LANCP SET DEV EWA0/SPEED=100
          ^^^
	  RSX LIVES!

