[...]
> You probably also want to set it in SRM too:
> 
> 	>>> set ewa0_mode fast


        This is good advice for  both  DU and OpenVMS.  Other choices to
    be used as appropriate are:

 	>>> set ewa0_mode fastfd            ...for full duplex

    and

 	>>> set ewa0_mode auto-sense        ...to auto-negotiate the speed

    Check with your networking folks  about  whether  the "other end" is
    set   to  full-  or  half-duplex,  and  whether  they  expect  auto-
    negotiation to work.

        However, I  would  ask  _which_  network  adapters  are  in your
    (Paul's)  AS4100's?   DE450's  which have AUI, ThinNet  and  10BaseT
    connectors _won't_ do Fast  Ethernet.   You  need  to  replace  them
    DE450's  with  DE500-BA's  for  example  (and,  on OVMS, you'll need
    either VMS 7.2 or 7.1 plus ECO's...don't know about VMS 6.2).

        -Ken
