    You're talking about the Base license, these are "concurrent user"
licenses. You first need a valid base license, then you add the number
of concurrent user licenses you require. VAXStation licensing is a
different situation as you aren't allowed to have more than 1 user
on a VAXStation.

    You're also talking about an update license ( which upgrades an
existing license to the current version ), the prices I quoted were
for new licenses.

    Having said all that, I find it surprising that an Update license
for a VAXStation 4000VLC would cost $10,000. It is pretty common for
sales types to quote the wrong part number though ( there are over
200 variants of the QL-001* part number ). What part number were
you quoted. Even better, what is the part number on the PAK for your
existing VMS license?

    OTOH, you could try using that price quote as justification to
get yourself a new DS10, with a VMS license, for less money :-)

