In my previous response, I forgot to add :

While in single user mode, edit /etc/passwd and /etc/group to remove
the '+:' line; this will limit logins to entries in the /etc/passwd
file only.  You might also want to remove any ',yp' references from
/etc/svc.conf .  Running the /usr/sbin/setup script(s) will do this for
you, but I'm giving the quick-and-dirty approach only.

