A channelserver is a VAX3400 system with 16 MB memory and
an IBM parallel channel interface for the S/370 or S/390 mainframes.
AKA the bus and tag interface.
It connects to the Digital environment via ethernet.

What it does is convert DECnet based applications to SNA applications.
The following applications are available:
=terminal emulation (CTERM-3270)
=RJE
=printer emulation

The mainframe must run MVS (now OS/390) or VSE and have VTAM support
(their network component).

We've been using a channelserver since 1991. It is still in use but no
longer in
a production environment since October.
Down time owing to software problems: 1 hour
Owing to hardware problems : 0 hours (hardware problems ? what's that)

Not easy to set up and maintain but a very nice piece of equipment to
connect
two entirely different architectures.

