> Clair Grant <grant@evms.zko.dec.com> writes:
> 
> 
>> I'm trying to get the automatic daylight savings change into the base OS
>> in the next release.
> 
>  You will test it in the southern hemisphere, right? And not
> forget that WA has NO DST.

I am not sure what difference the Southern Hemisphere makes, but there
are plenty of odd examples in the US.  The state of Arizona in general
does not do DST, but the Navajo Nation (Native American reservation
taking up about 1/6 of the area within Arizona) does do DST.

Obviously people who set their machines to GMT do not want it to change
either.  (GMT is an older time standard than UTC, intended for those who
do not run around adjusting their clocks to compensate for drift in the
earth's orbit. :-)

Larry Kilgallen



