I don't know -- but I think people misunderstood what I was talking about
before.

DEC has recently shipped some boxes with "Linux only" SRM -- normal SRM,
except that the systype reported to the operating system isn't one that
Digital Unix will recognize and run on.  To run DU, they give you new SRM
(for some boxes) if/when you pay a big upgrade fee.  For other boxes (e.g.
Alphaserver 330x) there isn't any SRM that will run DU at all, even though
the machines are totally normal examples of a systype that DU would, if it
were reported correctly, run on, e.g. the AlphaServer 1200.  This is the SRM
that's on some of the "white box" formerly NT-only Alphas that have been seen
up for auction lately.  I don't know if VMS will run with this SRM or not,
nor do I know if it's in fact what's on these budget "Linux Screams on..."
DS10s, but since it runs Linux or NetBSD just fine, there's no way to be
sure it isn't without ordering a box and trying to boot VMS or DU on it.

