I just got my DS5000/200 from Ebay today, went out and actually found an 
HD50 SCSI-2 cable to 50 pin dsub at Best Buy for $35. I get home hook up the
scsi to an external HD case I've had laying around, connect my Mac using a
high speed Mini-8 to RS-232 male cable, into a gender changer and into
serial port 3 on the back of the DS. Flip the power switch, power light
comes on in the front of the system, the red LED banks start to do there
thing, but nothing comes up on my screen. I switched it off and tried Serial
2, nothing. Thinking that cable might be bad I tried a DB9 serial to DEC MMJ
cable I made up into a DEC MMJ to RS-232 adapter, nothing on either port.
 I disconnected everything (COM and SCSI) and all the red LED's eventually
turned off (I am guessing that means it is at the console prompt) But if I
connect either SCSI or COM three of the red LED's stay on unless I hit the
halt key and they eventually do shut off.
  It has a PMAG-C display card with VRAM expansion (I haven't found any spec
or info on the card) And Four sticks of RAM in it. I tried pulling the Frame
buffer and mixing up the memory sticks, still nothing. In the process of
doing so I noticed that several of the small 24 pin square AMD chips between
the CPU and the memory banks were throwing off some serious heat. I could
feel the heat radiating from them with my hand above them. Touching them was
nearly to the point of melting skin. I assume this is not normal and the
system is probably dead. Any ideas/suggestions/rituals I should try?


Chris



