  variety of different multicast addresses, and later drivers need adapt 
  to the addresses set up by earlier drivers -- I would not expect this
  to work as a licensing scheme.  Some platforms -- DECnet Phase IV
  among them -- did have specific driver sequencing requirements.  (These 
  requirements were not tied to licensing.)

:I don't know if the OSF/1 boxes have real serial
:numbers in them somewhere or not.

  Alpha systems -- running Tru64 UNIX or otherwise -- do not include 
  serial numbers.

