I'm associated with a group that has come into some windfall money for
buying a machine for scientific computing.  For the most part, the group
has single processor Fortran code, but wants to move in the direction of
parallel code ( domain decomposition with message passing model ). The
consensus, by default, has centered around an SGI 8 processor Origin
2000 system.

For about the same price, we could get 2 ES40's with the TruCluster
software and interconnect.  For the legacy code, we would have the
advantage of much faster single processor speed, even against a promised
400 Mhz R12K upgrade for the Origin. 

I would like some comments ( amunition ) about how well the clustering
software works, how much the sysadmin costs might be relative to Origin
Irix, and whether there are any bottlenecks to multi-processor
performance for clean message passing parallel code.

Thanks,
John



