I am glad to hear that the DS10s do not have such SRM.  If you'll
go read what I actually wrote -- twice -- you'll note that I did *not*
say that the "killer deal" DS10s had such SRM, only that it would
probably make sense to make sure that they didn't before buying!

Perhaps you should consult the SRM development engineers instead of
the DS10 product manager.  They'll surely remember altering the systype
in several boxes' SRM so that Digital Unix wouln't run.

