There certainly is.  Look at the SRM for an AlphaServer 330x (a.k.a
AS1200, but reports a systype deliberately borked so DU won't use it)
or one of the 2100 variants originally sold as a "white box" NT
machine.  When SRM for these was made publically available -- only
a year ago now! -- it had had the systype modified so that it would
work with Linux but would *not* work with DU.  This clearly wasn't
done to "only support VMS", because leaving out the UNIX PALcode
would have been the obvious way to do that.  In fact, discussions
NetBSD developers had with DEC and API people involved confirmed
that "Linux only firmware" was intended to be the kinder, gentler
version of the previously announced NT-only borked MMU that, thank
goodness, never shipped on any 21164A parts.  This was the 'party
line' from these people even a few months ago, well after the
21264 launch.

If Compaq killed this insane policy, great!  But don't pretend it
didn't exist.

