>  [It is certainly NOT the case with the AlphaServer DS10 system.]  If
>  there are any more specifics around these "Linux only" SRM systems, I 
>  would be interested in hearing about it -- I am unaware of such boxes.

Now you've got the specifics you wanted, and I've got the ones I
wanted.  I completely fail to understand why my inquiry about this
very legitimate issue spawned such outrage.  Why, Nigel Barker
from Compaq even sent me a rather nasty piece of email that claimed
I was deliberately making false accusations.  Evidently he was not
aware that DEC had perpetrated the borked SRM in the past -- and that
it had been an active project as recently as a few months ago! -- but 
found it easier to flame me than to simply indicate that there was no 
such firmware for the DS10.  Nice way to answer my question.  Really 
nice.

Really makes me want to buy stuff from Compaq in the future.  One
of these actually _was_ on my shopping list for this quarter but
I'll surely cross it off now!

