Or to put it another way, the presentation "here's our spin, here's where
we are going, blah, blah, blah" isn't likely to be considered news unless
it's actually accompanied by an action of some significance.  I know the
sort of action I'd like to see ($2k base system: 128 Mb, 4gb scsi 500 Mhz
Alpha + $500K OpenVMS - includes everything in the Hobbyist CD) which would
be newsworthy even for the most jaded of IT journalists.  (The infoweek
headline: "Compaq: in your face Wintel!".  A guy can dream...)  However,
given Compaq's continued high end focus for VMS that doesn't seem likely.
Compaq would at least obtain better coverage of their current blah blah
blah if they'd synchronize it well with the release of a major piece of
hardware.  Or they could even put some backspin on an error and get some
positive publicity out of it: "Compaq admits slow delivery of DS10 systems
due to unexpectedly high demand."  

There hasn't been much out of Compaq lately in any case. The register had a
headline last week, something like "Compaq silence deafens the universe." 
It described how Compaq wasn't talking to them or any other IT journalists
the register polled. 

