On Fri, 01 Oct 1999 11:33:29 -0600, Kevin Handy <kth@srv.net> wrote:

>I've been trying to configure an Alpha 200 4/100 so that I can
>use Motif on it (Hobbyest License). So far, I've had to get
>a video card (Number 9), more memory (Total 96Mb now), but now
>the monitors I have don't seem to want to sync up to the video
>card.

Are you sure that you have the correct #9 card?. The #9 FX Motion 331 is the
analogue of the PB2GA-JC/JD & is based on the S3 Trio64V+ graphics chipset The
#9 FX Motion 330 is the analogue of the PB2GA-JA/JB based on the S3 Trio64.

>What characteristics are required for the Number 9 video card?
>Or is there some switch on the OpenVMS 7.2 that will use
>a lower resolution that my monitor can handle (which works
>at 1024 x 768 under windows), or is my video card broke?
>(Text mode works perfectly though)

The fact that you have tried multiple monitors implies that the graphics card is
wrong or broken. A variety of S3 based graphics cards will work in text mode. A
1MB video memory card will work in 1024 x 768.

Does Motif actually start? There will be an error log file in SYS$MANAGER the
name which escapes me for the moment (some permutation of DECW ERROR & LOG I
expect). My suspicion is that you will find something to the effect that no
supported device is found. Check that the graphics device GQA0: exists.


--
