I know that all the documentation says self discovery or self configuring
but!

In the SRM console, specifically set the ewa0_mode to what you want the
thing to talk to, be it, 10baseT or 100Mbps. Far too often a glitch happens,
the network stalls and the hardware goes back through an attempt to figure
out the media and then the speed of communication. This can take seconds and
in fact if one reads the manuals, systems that have more than one ethernet
interface, it is recomended that you set each interface up manually. This
avoids alot of wasted boot time doing auto-configuration.

