Oh there are plenty of utilities that were written to do this for you. And
every VMS system manager knows that you can change the value of the system
clock on the fly. My complaints are as follows:

1. you shouldn't have to change the clock if all the machines in the world
where synced to UTC
2. there are some applications that will get messed up if the clock is
changed while they are running (comparing the 64 bit starting time of a job
with the 64 bit ending time is much nicer if the clock wasn't manually
changed in between)

p.s. I too, was doing OpenVMS system management 13 years ago (VMS 4.4) but
the world has changed significantly since then.  Many of these machines are
now tied together (via the internet) and it seems that people are accessing
them from all over the world at all times of the day and night.

