>handskake.

Someone else here will likely know, but I don't think the above indicate
any significant problems.  They're likely just termination issues on the
SCSI or ethernet devices, or maybe related to the console wiring if you're
using a serial console on the box.

>2.) Can it run NetBSD? I can't seem to find the m46 or whatever model number
>anywhere on the system that corresponds to the VS3100's that it is
>compatible with.

Yes.  This box will be a vanilla VAXstation 3100/M30 unless it's in a
larger case which would make it an M40.  The systems are identical apart
from the enclosure size.

See: ftp://ftp.NetBSD.ORG/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-1.4.1/vax/  for the 1.4.1
release and related details.  You can create a bootable disk image using
the boot.fs.gz under the installation directory.

Another option is to boot the system over the network.

