Something a little strange...

I replaced a HSC50 running CRONIC Ver 4.1 with a HSC70 running a 'straight
out of the box'  Ver 8.3, which I configured to the
same ID etc as the HSC50.  The 50 was unplugged and wheeled away, and the 70
put in it's place.  It booted and could see all it's drives etc etc.
Unfortunately the Vax refused to boot from it.  No online light came up on
the HSC and the vax spat it with an
"error initialising I/O device" error.   I went to an earlier version (6.0)
of the HSC software, with the same config etc and got the same
result.  After much tinkering, I found that it worked if I set the CI node
number to 1 instead of 0, (SET ID %X00000000FE01 instead of to the HSC50's
SET ID %X00006215FF00 - The CPU id seems to make no difference one way or
the other.)  I changed the Vax boot command accordingly of course.   It
appears the 70 isn't happy being node 0 on the CI (the Vax is node 3, btw).
The HSC50 has been working fine as node 0 for 2 years.   No big deal now,
it's working, but I see nothing in the release notes or HSC manual that says
it can't be node 0.  Anyone know what I've done wrong here?  If anything?  I
will supply HSC SHO ALL listings if needed....

