Glen,

The Starion 900 main logic board was designed to support up to a
133MHz Pentium.  The following jumper settings are used to set the
procesor speed:

Main Logic Board Jumper Settings

Feature 	Description 	Setting
CPU clock 	50 MHz		J22, open
				J21, open
		60 MHz		J22, open
				J21, jumpered
		66 MHz		J22, jumpered
				J21, jumpered
CPU core/bus frequency 2/1 	J27, jumpered
		3/2		J27, open

You may also have some luck with faster processors (AMD, IDT, Intel
MMX), mostly in conjunction with a good quality processor adapter like
a PowerLeap.  I have a Starion 900 in my warehouse, but I haven't yet
tried anything faster than a 133.  Only so many hours in the day.

I'm also not sure yet if the Starion main logic board could be swapped
out for another low-profile LPX form factor board with Socket 7 and
more SIMM sockets.

... Ben Myers

