:I recently picked up an old vaxstation 3100 and the hobbyist
:CD/licenses. I've had a problem I'm hoping you can help me
:with. The VMS install (7.2) went fine and I was able to get
:a couple of compilers installed. I can compile a "hello.c"
:test to get a hello.obj. Trying to LINK HELLO, however,
:fails *only sometimes* with a Fatal Bugcheck called DELCONPFN
:
:Can anybody tell me what, exactly, is going wrong? LINK.EXE
:seems to be the only program/executable that does it...

  LINK is probably the only thing you are using that is churning
  through virtual memory.

  I would initially guess you might have a hardware problem with
  the system, though there is also a chance that this is an odd 
  (kernel-mode) software problem.  Check for overheating or bad
  fans, for loose connections, for an over-long or unterminated 
  SCSI, and for the other sorts of things that can cause a system 
  to encounter intermittent problems...

  Which particular VAXstation 3100 model?

  Has AUTOGEN been run on this system?  (If not, clean out the
  cruft in MODPARAMS.DAT and run it.  Then reboot.)

  I will assume you know about the system disk capacity limitation 
  found on all members of the VAXstation 3100 series.  If not, please
  see the OpenVMS FAQ for details.

