Organization: Southwest Cyberport
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=US-ASCII
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

hello
From the decsystem 5500 operations manual
at the >>> you may do the following
continue - returns control to the processes interrupted by a halt signal
boot - boots the operating system
d - deposits data at a given address
dump - dumps memory to the screen
e examine memory
exit - Exits maintenance mode and returns control to normal console mode
fill - deposits data in an address range
go resumes execution of the program in memory
help - displays the syntax of console commands
? - same as helop
init - reinitializes memroy
maint - causes the console to enter maintenance mode
passwd - allows you to use the console security feature
printenv - displays console environment variables
setenv- sets console environment variables
show device - displays a list of available devices, their unit numbers,
and controller numbers
show dssi - displays a list of available dssi storage devices, their unit
numbers, and controller numbers
show ethernet - displays the hardware address of your ethernet controller
show scsi - displays a list of available scsi storage devices, their unit
numbers, and controller numbers
unpriv - sets the security password to zero
unsetenv - unsets console environment variables

the following commands are available only in maintenane mode
exit, show device, show dssi, show ethernet, show scsi, unpriv

Since you remove the KFQSA (the dssi controller) and the TK70
controller I would go into maint and see what you system has.

hope this helps
phillip

OLD VAXs never die they just fade away




