All OS's running on Alpha keep date and time differently from each other.
When you change from one OS to another such as OpenVMS Tru64 UNIX or Windows
NT or LIUNX, you must reset the date and time inside the OS. There is not
much point in setting the date and time at the console as this will not
properly propogate to the OS at boot time. Remember for UNIX, you must be in
single user mode and have to issue a special command to re-sync the home
block.

Those useers with systems that contain an EISA bus must also run the EISA
configuration utility to prevent problems form occuring.

