>be operated by hand. It gets the power via a small plug from the circuit
>board. Removing this plug and applying a current from an external low
>voltage supply (3-5V) ejects the tape.

All the TLZ04 drives I have used had a hole on the left hand side of the
drive mechanism covered by a sticky plastic patch.  Removing that patch
exposes a gear that is part of the ejection mechanism.  Turning it with
a screwdriver or fingernail the right direction will eject the cartridge
from the drive.  Do this with the power off of course.

Joe Heimann

heimann@ecs.umass.edu

(Had to remove quite a few tapes from TLZ04's over the years.)



