DECsystem 5500

   The DECsystem 5500 is shipped in a BA430 enclosure, which provides a
   12-slot backplane and room for four mass storage devices. The base
   system contains the following:
     * A KN220-AA module set. This consists of a KN220 I/O module in slot
       1 and a KN220 CPU module in slot 2.
       The CPU module contains:
          + 30 MHz R3000 CPU with R3010 FPU.
          + 512 kBytes of Prestoserve battery backed RAM.
       The I/O module contains:
          + Q22-bus interface
          + SGEC Second Generation Ethernet Controller
          + DSSI Digital Storage System Interconnect port
          + SII-based SCSI port.
     * From 1 to 4 MS220-AA 32MB memory modules, installed in slots 3
       through 7.
       64MB memory modules are also available (part number?).

... so it looks like a VAX with a MIPS CPU :-). This machine is not 
supported by NetBSD (and also not by OpenBSD or DECstation Linux), so 
your only OS choice will be Ultrix.

